    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="1157" n="999" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg999"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Japanese
                    Chargé</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January 10,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Hioki</hi>: I send you informally a copy
                    of a letter<anchor n="a" xml:id="d134-f1"/> from the Secretary of Agriculture
                    communicating one to him from Mr. B. F. Tillinghast, of Davenport, Iowa, stating
                    that the Davenport Democrat would feel it a duty to invite subscriptions and
                    apply them in such manner as your legation might authorize to relieve the
                    suffering caused by famine in the northeastern provinces of Japan.</p>
                <p>The department has no advices on the subject of the alleged famine, and I
                    therefore beg to inquire whether the situation is, in fact, so serious that
                    outside contributions would be acceptable.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
